  "summary": {
    "en": "US forces have begun a land operation against cartels inside Ecuador while President Noboa asked the United States for $430.5 billion in security aid and met with Pete Hegseth on anti-narco cooperation. Noboa rejected claims that former vice president Jorge Glas was tortured, saying his injuries were self-inflicted. Journalist Omar Toledo was shot by motorcycle gunmen and wounded. Commander Willy, a fugitive gang boss, was arrested at a hotel in Sitges and deported from Spain. The UCDP recorded two battle-related deaths in 2019, according to UCDP.",
    "nb": "US-styrker har startet en landoperasjon mot karteller i Ecuador mens president Noboa ba USA om $430.5 milliarder i sikkerhetsstøtte og møtte Pete Hegseth om anti-narko-samarbeid. Noboa avviste påstander om at tidligere visepresident Jorge Glas ble torturert, og sa at hans skader var selvpåførte. Journalisten Omar Toledo ble skutt av motorcykel-skyttere og såret. Kommandør Willy, en påflukt gjengleder, ble arrestert på et hotell i Sitges og deportert fra Spania. UCDP registrerte to kamprelaterte dødsfall i 2019, ifølge UCDP.",
